  "term": "confirmatory factor analysis",
  "definition": "Confirmatory factor analysis is a statistical method used to test whether data fit an expected factor structure in a measure. In this study, it was used to examine whether the stigma scale matched a proposed two-factor model and whether the model showed acceptable fit.",
